<article class="env-lemma" id="08D2">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/08D2">Lemma <span data-tag="08D2">36.9.4</span>.</a> In Situation <a href="/tag/08CZ" data-tag="08CZ">36.9.1</a>. Let $\mathcal{F}^\bullet $ be a complex of quasi-coherent $\mathcal{O}_ X$-modules. Then there is a canonical isomorphism </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \text{Tot}(\check{\mathcal{C}}_{alt}^\bullet (\mathcal{U}, \mathcal{F}^\bullet )) \longrightarrow R\Gamma (U, \mathcal{F}^\bullet )  \]
</div>
  <p> in $D(A)$ functorial in $\mathcal{F}^\bullet $. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $\mathcal{B}$ be the set of affine opens of $U$. Since the higher cohomology groups of a quasi-coherent module on an affine scheme are zero (Cohomology of Schemes, Lemma <a href="/tag/01XB" data-tag="01XB">30.2.2</a>) this is a special case of Cohomology, Lemma <a href="/tag/08C2" data-tag="08C2">20.40.2</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>